lity, calmness, technical competence, and positive atmosphere, despite communication difficulty which may be mitigated. He could propose C as leading candidate, and note that D's arrogance and hot temper are more severe for crew cooperation. He could also note B's memory issues.\n\nThus James changes his vote to Candidate C. Provide evidence: reliability 100%, correct decisions quickly, calm in crisis, understands technology, excellent attention, creates positive atmosphere. Also note concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Argue that these are less severe than D's arrogance/hot temper and B's nasty remarks.\n\nMake public message: \"I appreciate Sarah's points, but I think Candidate C is stronger overall.\" Provide reasoning. Then metadata vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
