el, James currently voted Candidate C. He may keep his vote, but must provide argument. Also need to address remaining candidate A not discussed yet. He could bring up A as a point, but must keep focus. Perhaps he can say he still supports C, but we need to discuss A before final decision. Provide a brief note that A hasn't been discussed and we need to evaluate. But must keep contribution focused. He can say: I agree with Emily, maintain C, but note we still need to consider A. Provide some of his own facts about A: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, but regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas, unorganized, not good at taking criticism, unhealthy eating. He can argue that these concerns make A less suitable. So he can keep vote C.\n\nThus public message: agree with Emily, maintain C, note A's concerns, and suggest we can move toward final decision if no further concerns.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
