e could also bring up A's strengths and weaknesses, and perhaps argue that C remains best. She must state her vote. According to shared mental model, she currently voted D, but after new evidence, she may change to C. She should provide reasoning: D's arrogance and weak leadership are serious crew cooperation concerns, while C's reliability and positive atmosphere outweigh his communication difficulty. Also note A's issues. So she will shift vote to C.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I agree with James and Emily, and now recommend Candidate C. While D has strong responsibility and problem solving, his arrogance and weak leadership raise crew cooperation concerns. Candidate C's 100% reliability, quick correct decisions, calmness, technical competence, excellent attention, and positive crew atmosphere outweigh his communication difficulty. Candidate A also has concerns. Therefore I shift my vote to C.\"\n\nMetadata: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
